-- =========================================================================
-- Email — the `EmailService` CAPABILITY, authored as a Fenel record-of-methods
-- type (module-substrate Phase 3k follow-up: "typeclasses ARE types" on a real
-- capability, no TS `ClassSeed` const).
--
-- A capability is a record whose fields are its methods (each an arrow type) —
-- the same shape `fenel/std/algebra.fenel` declares Functor/Monad/Monoid. The
-- email seam reads this type and `seedFromType`s it into the dispatch
-- `ClassSeed` (replacing the retired hand-written const). `EmailService` is
-- NOMINAL — it is dispatched by PROVIDER NAME via `resolveCapabilityMethod`
-- (which splits a qualified `EmailService.<method>` action and picks the
-- highest-priority provider instance), NOT by `seedFromType`'s effect-dispatch
-- arg-position path; no method carries a class type-param in argument position.
-- So the derived seed needs only the right method NAMES + signatures (proven:
-- `seedFromType` yields `[send, send_batch, suppress, domainAdd, domainVerify,
-- domainList]` with the declared returns).
--
-- The capability NAME is `EmailService`, NOT `Email`: `getType("Email")` must
-- stay undefined so the data `Email` (in `email.fenel`) routes to the catalog
-- "entity" section, not "spec" (Phase 3.4b).
--
-- METHOD NAMES are plain idents. The three domain operations were named with
-- literal dots (`domain.add` / `domain.verify` / `domain.list`) in the retired
-- TS — a cosmetic faux-namespace that `.fenel` record keys (plain idents; `.`
-- is field-access) cannot carry. Renamed to `domainAdd` / `domainVerify` /
-- `domainList`: the dotted strings were internal-only (the capability method
-- name → the IO-handler key → the `PROVIDER_IMPLS` lookup, all self-derived;
-- nothing external/persisted references them), so the rename is fully
-- behaviour-preserving and was applied across the providers + the runtime
-- `PROVIDER_IMPLS` map + the tests in one change. `send_batch` keeps its
-- underscore (a valid ident — only the DOTTED names needed renaming).
--
-- This file is loaded SEPARATELY from `email.fenel` (NOT merged) so the
-- `EmailService` type does not enter `emailModule.entities` (which is the
-- 14-data-type roster); the seam reads only its type to derive the seed.
-- =========================================================================

EmailService = EmailService send: (Email -> SendResult) send_batch: ([Email] -> [SendResult]) suppress: (Address -> String -> {}) domainAdd: (String -> SendingDomain) domainVerify: (String -> SendingDomain) domainList: [SendingDomain]
